@startuml System_Failover_Flow
title System Failover — Database Shard Primary Failure
autonumber

participant "Health Monitor (Patroni)" as MON
database "Primary (Shard N)" as PRIM
database "Replica (Shard N)" as REPL
participant "PgBouncer (Connection Pool)" as PGB
participant "Application Services" as APP
participant "Circuit Breaker\nCB-DB-PRIMARY" as CB
participant "On-call Engineer" as ONCALL

APP -> PGB: write request (via primary)
PGB -> PRIM: forward write
PRIM --> PGB: **no response — connection timeout**

APP -> CB: write request
CB -> CB: 2 failures / 5s threshold reached -> **OPEN**
CB --> APP: fallback: queue write, route reads to replica

MON -> PRIM: heartbeat check
PRIM --> MON: **no response (missed heartbeats)**
MON -> MON: declare primary DOWN
MON -> REPL: promote to new PRIMARY
REPL --> MON: promotion complete

MON -> PGB: update routing config -> new primary
PGB --> MON: ACK

MON -> ONCALL: send P1 alert (immediate page, 5-min SLA)

note over MON, REPL: Target: complete failover within 30s (NFR-006 RTO)

CB -> CB: reset timeout expires (10s) -> **HALF-OPEN**, probe request
CB -> PGB: probe write
PGB -> REPL: forward write (now acting as primary)
REPL --> PGB: write OK
CB -> CB: probe succeeded -> **CLOSED**
CB --> APP: resume normal writes

APP -> APP: retry queued writes\n(idempotency keys prevent any duplicate processing)

note over PRIM: Old primary rejoins the cluster later as a new REPLICA —\nnot immediately re-promoted, to avoid split-brain risk\n(mitigates FMEA item FM-004).
@enduml
